inet: annotate data-races around isk->inet_num

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.4.1.el9_9
commit-author Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
commit 29252397bcc1e0a1f85e5c3bee59c325f5c26341
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.4.1.el9_9/29252397.failed

UDP/TCP lookups are using RCU, thus isk->inet_num accesses
should use READ_ONCE() and WRITE_ONCE() where needed.

Fixes: 3ab5aee7fe84 ("net: Convert TCP & DCCP hash tables to use RCU / hlist_nulls")
	Signed-off-by: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
	Reviewed-by: Kuniyuki Iwashima <kuniyu@google.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260225203545.1512417-1-edumazet@google.com
	Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 29252397bcc1e0a1f85e5c3bee59c325f5c26341)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/ipv4/inet_hashtables.c
#	net/ipv4/tcp_diag.c
